{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"02d580fbcbce5e68","name":"card_event_ski_troops","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_ski_troops","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SKI TROOPS","text":"When the enemy deploys a unit, suppress it, then add a SISSI to your support line.","flavorText":"When the Soviet Union invaded Finland in November 1939, Finnish ski troops quickly emerged as one of the defining forces of the Winter War. Outnumbered and lacking heavy equipment, they leveraged their skis, white winter camouflage, and deep knowledge of the forests to run circles around road-bound Soviet formations. This extreme mobility was the cornerstone of the Finnish motti tactics. Ski troops would strike the front and rear of long, vulnerable Soviet columns, chopping them into isolated pockets. Once trapped, these pockets were systematically dismantled using sniper fire, mortars, submachine guns, and Molotov cocktails. Beyond their physical toll, these sudden strikes inflicted heavy psychological damage. Gliding silently through the dense woods, Finnish soldiers would ambush camps and supply lines, melting back into the forest before the Soviets could even mount a response. At major engagements like the Battle of Suomussalmi, these hit-and-run tactics allowed vastly outnumbered Finnish forces to annihilate massive mechanized units, proving that speed and terrain mastery could overcome overwhelming numerical superiority.","faction":"Finland","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_ski_troops","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_ski_troops_title","SourceString":"SKI TROOPS","LocalizedString":"SKI TROOPS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_ski_troops_text","SourceString":"When the enemy deploys a unit, suppress it, then add a 